1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,986
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,036 --> 00:00:05,422
Tiny Coders, video 7.

3
00:00:05,472 --> 00:00:08,670
Guide a character on a grid.

4
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:14,246
Coders often move a character on a grid using forward and turn

5
00:00:14,296 --> 00:00:16,900
— the same idea as many coding games.

6
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:21,618
Forward moves one square the way you face.

7
00:00:21,668 --> 00:00:25,849
Turn left or right changes direction without moving.

8
00:00:25,899 --> 00:00:30,080
The goal is to reach the star without hitting walls.

9
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:32,675
Try it on paper.

10
00:00:32,725 --> 00:00:36,661
Draw a four by four grid, mark a start and a star,

11
00:00:36,711 --> 00:00:39,530
and write the fewest moves you need.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,271
Let us recap.

13
00:00:42,321 --> 00:00:45,522
Grid moves are forward and turn.

14
00:00:45,572 --> 00:00:48,774
Shorter plans are often clearer.

15
00:00:48,824 --> 00:00:52,940
Next: Project: invent a 5-step robot job.
